I wrote in my diary about my trip to Odense.
It was a lovely Saturday morning.
I woke up early, already at seven o'clock.
The sun was shining, and the sky was blue.
I packed my small, green backpack.
I put a notebook and a camera in the bag.
I also brought a thick sweater.
The spring weather in Denmark can be a bit cold.
Then I took the bus into the large station in Copenhagen.
There were many busy people inside.
I walked over to a small kiosk.
I bought a large, warm coffee for the trip.
It cost forty-five kroner.
I looked up at the large screen.
I quickly found my train on the screen.
I was taking the fast train to Odense.
The train arrived at the platform exactly at eight o'clock.
I went into the train and found my seat by a large window.
I drank my warm coffee and looked forward to the excursion.
